(2563981, 348886, 19944, '<td valign="top">So to answer some of the questions:<br/> <br/>1.) No this is not identical triplets.  This is just one person, my youngest daughter.<br/>2.) Some people''s comments were inferring that this may be a self portrait.  See #1 above.<br/>3.) How I did it: I set up the camera on a tripod, facing my basement couch.  I hung a big piece of black felt on the wall behind and drapped over the couch.  I had my daughter sit on the couch so I could manually focus the camera, I set it for manual exposure at 30" seconds and f8.  I had her move along the couch so I could get a good idea what positions she should sit in.  Luckily, we could use the edges of the cushions as a guide.  I hung a white umbrella from the ceiling, so I could bounce my flash toward her.  I turned out the lights, she took her first position, I hit the shutter on the camera and I held my flash above my head, toward the umbrella and fired.  I had her move to the next position, and fired the flash again.  Then a third time.<br/> <br/>I only took about eight shots.  Initially, I only did two flashes, with her basically looking at herself.  The lighting didn''t come out right, and you couldn''t really see her face.  Then we tried three of her, the one in the middle facing forward and the ones on the sides looking at her.  This time there was a lot of overlap.  FInally, she suggested the hear, see, speak no evil thing.  This took two takes, just to get the positioning right.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the nice comments, and I hope I didn''t lose too many points for having them in the wrong order!<br/></td>', 'So to answer some of the questions: 1.) No this is not identical triplets.  This is just one person, my youngest daughter.2.) Some people''s comments were inferring that this may be a self portrait.  See #1 above.3.) How I did it: I set up the camera on a tripod, facing my basement couch.  I hung a big piece of black felt on the wall behind and drapped over the couch.  I had my daughter sit on the couch so I could manually focus the camera, I set it for manual exposure at 30" seconds and f8.  I had her move along the couch so I could get a good idea what positions she should sit in.  Luckily, we could use the edges of the cushions as a guide.  I hung a white umbrella from the ceiling, so I could bounce my flash toward her.  I turned out the lights, she took her first position, I hit the shutter on the camera and I held my flash above my head, toward the umbrella and fired.  I had her move to the next position, and fired the flash again.  Then a third time. I only took about eight shots.  Initially, I only did two flashes, with her basically looking at herself.  The lighting didn''t come out right, and you couldn''t really see her face.  Then we tried three of her, the one in the middle facing forward and the ones on the sides looking at her.  This time there was a lot of overlap.  FInally, she suggested the hear, see, speak no evil thing.  This took two takes, just to get the positioning right. Thanks for the nice comments, and I hope I didn''t lose too many points for having them in the wrong order!', '2006-06-28 21:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2564035, 349098, 11518, '<td valign="top">Great idea, but what would have made it stand out more was to see more definition in the hands.  I would have kept still for about 15 seconds then started typing...This way the photo would have shown the hands more and get the movement for the last 15 seconds.</td>', 'Great idea, but what would have made it stand out more was to see more definition in the hands.  I would have kept still for about 15 seconds then started typing...This way the photo would have shown the hands more and get the movement for the last 15 seconds.', '2006-06-28 21:44:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2564066, 349098, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few thoughts:<br/>1) The tight crop is tough.  I see why you did it, but it may have been the lesser of two evils.  It doesn''t help, it just may hurt less.<br/>2) The idea is neat, but in the end you may have done about as much with it as you could.  If you wanted more fingers, you should have tried typing S-L-O-W-E-R. :)<br/>3) The conversion to B&amp;W is decent.</td>', 'A few thoughts:1) The tight crop is tough.  I see why you did it, but it may have been the lesser of two evils.  It doesn''t help, it just may hurt less.2) The idea is neat, but in the end you may have done about as much with it as you could.  If you wanted more fingers, you should have tried typing S-L-O-W-E-R. :)3) The conversion to B&W is decent.', '2006-06-28 21:55:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2564072, 349238, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few things come to mind here:<br/>1) I think people were looking for some effect as a result of the 30-second exposure.  While I hope people gave you the benefit of the doubt that the shot really WAS 30-seconds, they may ask, WHY was it 30-seconds.  It doesn''t really do much more for us than a 1/60th second exposure (with the proper light of course).<br/>2)  Blue is a tough color for skin.  She may be a sleeping beauty because she''s dead...;)<br/>3)  You managed to get some areas too light.  Namely her forehead and the crook of her elbow.<br/> <br/>Keep trying though.  I think the idea was creative.</td>', 'A few things come to mind here:1) I think people were looking for some effect as a result of the 30-second exposure.  While I hope people gave you the benefit of the doubt that the shot really WAS 30-seconds, they may ask, WHY was it 30-seconds.  It doesn''t really do much more for us than a 1/60th second exposure (with the proper light of course).2)  Blue is a tough color for skin.  She may be a sleeping beauty because she''s dead...;)3)  You managed to get some areas too light.  Namely her forehead and the crook of her elbow. Keep trying though.  I think the idea was creative.', '2006-06-28 21:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2564697, 350511, 75713, '<td valign="top">sorry i am late in adding my congrats.... I would have given this shot a 9 if I had of been around for the voting... wtg!</td>', 'sorry i am late in adding my congrats.... I would have given this shot a 9 if I had of been around for the voting... wtg!', '2006-06-29 01:04:09.000000', NULL, 0),
