(2565301, 349689, 35720, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot! Congratulations on being in third place, it is a great shot although it will probably be disqualified because you cloned out the sensor spot. I have said it in a discussion before and I''ll say it again here: It should be allowed to clean sensor spots in basic editing.</td>', 'Wonderful shot! Congratulations on being in third place, it is a great shot although it will probably be disqualified because you cloned out the sensor spot. I have said it in a discussion before and I''ll say it again here: It should be allowed to clean sensor spots in basic editing.', '2006-06-29 06:19:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2565367, 349419, 55838, '<td valign="top">I must admit that I believe you were robbed.  Although 85th percentile rocks on any day of the week.  26th place and a score north of 6 for your first entry (any entry for that matter) is just plain awesome.  Well done.  Adding this pic to my favorites.</td>', 'I must admit that I believe you were robbed.  Although 85th percentile rocks on any day of the week.  26th place and a score north of 6 for your first entry (any entry for that matter) is just plain awesome.  Well done.  Adding this pic to my favorites.', '2006-06-29 07:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2565615, 350213, 49202, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments and the faves, and a million sorries for my sucky notes.<br/> <br/>For those who care for specifics:<br/> <br/>This photo wasn''t taken with the challenge in mind.<br/>This shot was a photographic representation of what I was feeling at that moment.<br/> <br/>The obsured face, the slouch, the removed sandals, the TUNA shirt that should''ve been PUMA, and the bare unfinished room all deal with feelings of uncertainty and lack of self confidence.<br/> <br/>Counterbalancing the negativity are the centered composition, for stillness amidst chaos, and the wedding ring, for clarity of thought and strength of will -- as as of the date of shooting, I''ve been married for four days.<br/> <br/>The title was to say that whatever is being said was not in what was being shown. Even then, the photo is open to interpretation for those who wish to share its reality.<br/> <br/>P.S. The sucky photographer''s comments was the introvert half of me who finds baring one''s self, even in such an obscured manner, emo. Again, sorry for this.<br/> <br/><i>Edited just because.</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-05 22:25:34.</i></td>', 'Thank you for the comments and the faves, and a million sorries for my sucky notes. For those who care for specifics: This photo wasn''t taken with the challenge in mind.This shot was a photographic representation of what I was feeling at that moment. The obsured face, the slouch, the removed sandals, the TUNA shirt that should''ve been PUMA, and the bare unfinished room all deal with feelings of uncertainty and lack of self confidence. Counterbalancing the negativity are the centered composition, for stillness amidst chaos, and the wedding ring, for clarity of thought and strength of will -- as as of the date of shooting, I''ve been married for four days. The title was to say that whatever is being said was not in what was being shown. Even then, the photo is open to interpretation for those who wish to share its reality. P.S. The sucky photographer''s comments was the introvert half of me who finds baring one''s self, even in such an obscured manner, emo. Again, sorry for this. Edited just because.', '2006-06-29 09:45:29.000000', '2006-07-05 23:25:34.000000', 0),
(2565711, 349689, 18011, '<td valign="top">I hope i''ll not disqualified. I''ve used an alien skin plug-in to remove dust from entire image.<br/> <br/>Thanx for all visiting and comments!<br/> <br/>Gipo ;-D</td>', 'I hope i''ll not disqualified. I''ve used an alien skin plug-in to remove dust from entire image. Thanx for all visiting and comments! Gipo ;-D', '2006-06-29 10:52:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2565734, 349873, 19978, '<td valign="top">Dennis, I''d venture to say that fewer than 1 out of 1000 DPC users appreciate what this photo depicts and have no idea the difficulties involved in capturing the subtleties shown. Not only do you show the dust lanes leading into Sagittarius, but you''ve also captured the elusive nebulosities around Rho Oph. Superb work with a single exposure. From one astrophotographer to another, my hat is off. I''d love to see a link to a full size version, if you have one online.</td>', 'Dennis, I''d venture to say that fewer than 1 out of 1000 DPC users appreciate what this photo depicts and have no idea the difficulties involved in capturing the subtleties shown. Not only do you show the dust lanes leading into Sagittarius, but you''ve also captured the elusive nebulosities around Rho Oph. Superb work with a single exposure. From one astrophotographer to another, my hat is off. I''d love to see a link to a full size version, if you have one online.', '2006-06-29 10:57:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2566478, 348876, 60443, '<td valign="top">Just three words - gorgeous, gorgeous, gorgeous!</td>', 'Just three words - gorgeous, gorgeous, gorgeous!', '2006-06-29 14:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2566636, 350089, 50578, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and votes. <br/> <br/>Wow  no 1''s this time.   and 4 10''s  which I didn''t expect<br/> <br/>It was interesting to see how many people commented on the plane. Just goes to show how everyone sees things in a different perspective.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-29 14:31:30.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments and votes.  Wow  no 1''s this time.   and 4 10''s  which I didn''t expect It was interesting to see how many people commented on the plane. Just goes to show how everyone sees things in a different perspective.', '2006-06-29 15:30:21.000000', '2006-06-29 15:31:30.000000', 0),
(2566678, 351057, 52115, '<td valign="top">Thanks for not putting this in last place.<br/>I think if I spent more time it has potential. I''ll be back!<br/>Like the irridescent -foil covered tubes/funnel-top needed more light.<br/> <br/>This was taken upside down in a black box puppet theatre style. I slowly rotated a flashing, wierd ball, that''s shaped like an atom nucleous.<br/> <br/>And I created a 30-second .mp3 file in which I recorded my own voice counting-down. I played that on my iPod used as the audio-prompter for my timing.</td>', 'Thanks for not putting this in last place.I think if I spent more time it has potential. I''ll be back!Like the irridescent -foil covered tubes/funnel-top needed more light. This was taken upside down in a black box puppet theatre style. I slowly rotated a flashing, wierd ball, that''s shaped like an atom nucleous. And I created a 30-second .mp3 file in which I recorded my own voice counting-down. I played that on my iPod used as the audio-prompter for my timing.', '2006-06-29 15:50:55.000000', NULL, 0),
